1   The parsing of a config needs to be a recursive affair. 
    Parse classes rely on a map that supplies instances or child parse classes
    Parse class & map interaction
        - read its entity class into 3 tuple of key, type and value
            - members are either primitives which the parse class satisfies from its data dict
            - if type is not an entity, then it resolves from data
            - if type is an entity: 
                - returns the entity or returns a parse class to tackle its instatiation
    
class Mapclass():
    filelist_map 
    collector: ErrorCollector
    def set(self, entity_cls: type[Entity], key: str, value: Entity) -> None: ...
    def set[E: Entity](self, entity_cls: type[E], data: str | Any) -> E | BaseParser | None: ...

